Observed failure: In keyboard test step 6, they typed Atlantis into shipping country then cleared billing country etc. Expected shipping_country value "" but observed "gb". So the issue: typing unrecognized value leaves previous selection (UK) in hidden select.

Our earlier attempts tried adding sync listeners but didn't work because maybe the library overwrites after our listener? Need to ensure we set select value after library updates? Actually library likely sets the input value but not the select. Our listener runs on input/change/blur events of the autocomplete input. However the library might also listen to those events and update something else after ours? We need to ensure our handler runs after the library's update. Could use setTimeout to defer, or listen to 'autocomplete-select' event? Not sure.

Better approach: Instead of attaching to input/change/blur, we could override the library's enhanceSelectElement to also update select when input changes? But we cannot modify library file (hash must match). So we need to add listeners that fire after library's update. Perhaps listen to 'blur' after a short delay using setTimeout zero.

Alternatively, we could listen to the 'autocomplete-close' event? Not documented.

Simpler: Use 'input' event but set select.value after a microtask: queueMicrotask(() => { ... }) or setTimeout(fn,0).

