Root cause: accessible-autocomplete library does not update underlying <select> when user types unrecognized or blank value, causing previously selected option to remain.

Repair strategy: Add synchronization listeners that run after library's input events (using setTimeout) to set the hidden select's value based on input matching option label, otherwise empty.

Expected effect: Keyboard and screen‑reader users will see form data reflect exactly what is shown in each country field, allowing correct clearing of selections and preventing hidden stale values from being submitted.

Functional risks: Possible race if library updates after our timeout; but using setTimeout 0 ensures macro-task after current tick, low risk. Overriding valid selection if input temporarily non‑matching during composition, but events fire after composition ends.

